---
source: src/mcp/tools.rs
expression: SSH_EXEC_DESCRIPTION
---
Run a shell command on the preset's SSH host. The command must match one of the preset's `allowed_commands` regexes (anchored ^...$). Returns stdout, stderr, and exit_code. Key-based auth only; host key is verified against the user's known_hosts file. Sensitive presets trigger the approval prompt. If the user previously approved a time-boxed window for this preset+action, the call proceeds without a new prompt and is recorded as 'windowed' in the audit log. Every call is recorded to the audit log.
